\n\\[ h = 2.5r \\]\n\nSubstituting \\( h = 2.5r \\) into the surface area formula, we get:\n\\[ A = 2\\pi r^2 + 2\\pi r(2.5r) \\]\n\\[ A = 2\\pi r^2 + 5\\pi r^2 \\]\n\\[ A = 7\\pi r^2 \\]\n\nWe are also given that the surface area \\( A \\) is \\( 112\\pi \\) cm\\(^2\\). So we can set up the equation:\n\\[ 7\\pi r^2 = 112\\pi \\]\n\nTo find \\( r^2 \\), we divide both sides of the equation by \\( 7\\pi \\):\n\\[ r^2 = \\frac{112\\pi}{7\\pi} \\]\n\\[ r^2 = 16 \\]\n\nTaking the square root of both sides, we get:\n\\[ r = \\sqrt{16} \\]\n\\[ r = 4 \\]\n\nTherefore, the radius of the cylinder is \\(\\boxed{4}\\) cm."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{4}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:185"}
